   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "Full terrain map set (read me first)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "From noise to a complete set of terrain maps, all in COP, no AI, no mesh. Erosion is simulated at 512², the maps come out at 1024².\n\n① Shape: a hybrid terrain fractal + a Wrangle raises the middle into a mountain mass; Stream Power cuts dendritic river valleys, Strata makes rock-layer terraces, thermal erosion slumps into talus piles (debris), hydraulic erosion carves gullies and accumulates sediment into debris (this step is the slowest, over ten seconds on numpy; with CUDA it runs on the GPU automatically).\n\n② Water: Flow Accumulation computes the drainage area → river network river, filled depressions lake.\n\n③ Materials: Splat Map splits into five layers grass / sediment / rock / snow / water (summing to 1 everywhere), and also outputs splat_rgba (for the engine's terrain layers).\n\n④ Shading: normal, AO, shadows; a Wrangle mixes colours from the five layers (rock gets bands by height, wet areas are darkened), Light lights it with shadows. Also outputs a contour map.\n\nThe right column is all Save Image: height, normal, splat, albedo, final image."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
